{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"agent_message","text":"I submitted the mitigation; the endpoint accepted it at the mitigation stage.\n\nThe storefront's `/api/products` was returning 500s because product-catalog could not authenticate to Postgres (`password authentication failed for user \"otelu\"`). The `product-catalog-db-conn` secret was written at 01:01:39, after the pod was created at 01:01:35, so the running pod was likely still holding the old credential. The database accepts the secret's password, and every config in the namespace uses it.\n\nFix: I ran `kubectl rollout restart deploy/product-catalog -n astronomy-shop`. The new pod (`product-catalog-674d984688-j2zhr`) rolled out cleanly. Afterwards, `/api/products` and `/` returned 200 through `frontend-proxy`, and Postgres logged no new auth failures.\n\nNot changed, but worth a look:\n- The `product-catalog` memory limit is 64Mi, which is tight for the service.\n- The `product-reviews` deployment has a second revision whose DB password string differs from the rest of the config.\n- The `product-catalog` and `accounting` deployments have been modified outside Helm (`kubectl-set`, `OpenAPI-Generator`), so Helm state has drifted."}}
